  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You can apply this complication to a plan talent that involves gaining an item or piece of information. When you reveal the chosen plan talent, attempt a Knowledge or Lore check against the same DC required to gain the item or information (or as normal for a plan).</p>\n<p>If you succeed against this complication, you name two items or pieces of information that could be gained by the talent and the GM must tell you which one is more likely to be useful to you regarding the obstacles at hand that you could reasonably be aware of (or that they are about equally likely to be useful). After the GM’s response, you choose one of them to reveal with the plan.</p>\n<p>If you fail against this complication, you fail to gain the item or information, and it is obvious that there was an attempt to obtain the item or information through deceitful (or similar) means.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/study#toc22\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
